# Avoid Redundant Requests

If multiple components fetch the same data, you can cache the result. Use a simple cache map outside the composable.

```javascript
const cache = new Map()

export function useFetch(url) {
  if (cache.has(url)) {
    return { data: ref(cache.get(url)), loading: ref(false), error: ref(null) }
  }
  // ... fetch and store in cache
}
```

More sophisticated caching can include expiration times.

# Canceling In‑Flight Requests

If the component unmounts or the user triggers a new request before the previous one finishes, you should cancel the pending request to avoid race conditions.

```javascript
let controller

const fetchData = async () => {
  if (controller) controller.abort() // cancel previous
  controller = new AbortController()
  try {
    const res = await fetch(url, { signal: controller.signal })
    // ...
  } catch (err) {
    if (err.name !== 'AbortError') error.value = err.message
  }
}
```

Use `onUnmounted` to abort if the component is destroyed while fetching.
